"Q24: does a tail call stay constant-space in expression style as well as in guard style?"
"Run from the repo root:  cargo build -p interpreter --release && /usr/bin/time -l target/release/smol < docs/experiments/q24_tco_shapes.smol"
"Run one shape per invocation (comment the other out) and compare 'maximum resident set size'."

Object subclass: #Counter instanceVariableNames: ''.

"Guard style: ^ inside the ifTrue: block, then a method-level tail send."
Counter >> guard: n [ n = 0 ifTrue: [^0]. ^self guard: n - 1 ]

"Expression style: no ^ in any block; the tail send is the value of the ifFalse: branch."
Counter >> expr: n [ ^n = 0 ifTrue: [0] ifFalse: [self expr: n - 1] ]

(Counter new SHAPE: 3000000) await
